       mode = sb->s_root
               ? (S_IFDIR | (0777 & sbi->options->fs_dmask_inv))
               : (S_IFDIR | 0777);
   ```
   - This section enumerates attributes (`ATTR_ROOT`) and assigns directory semantics (`S_IFDIR` mode) if certain conditions are met. While it checks for specific valid attributes at one layer, there is **no validation of whether the record itself is appropriate to be treated as a directory**.

   **Step 3.4: Implicit Directory Handling via `ATTR_REPARSE`**:
   ```c
   case ATTR_REPARSE:
       if (attr->name_len)
           goto next_attr;

       rp_fa = ni_parse_reparse(ni, attr, &rp);
       switch (rp_fa) {
       case REPARSE_LINK:
           if (ni->ni_flags & NI_FLAG_DIR) {
